{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>But My servant Caleb</b> – He did not mention Joshua, because He specified Caleb's reward — that he would inherit the land upon which he came. And Joshua's reward is not fitting to be specified now, since it is that he would be in Moses' place. And Scripture gave precedence to \"but Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun\" (Numbers 14:30) because he it was who first took issue with the spies: \"And Caleb silenced\" (Numbers 13:30). But Moses said, \"Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh lived of those men\" (Numbers 14:38), because of the greatness of Joshua's rank in wisdom, and because Moses and Aaron fell on their faces before the entire assembly of the congregation of the children of Israel (Numbers 14:5) to entreat Him — the speech there was also to Aaron. And the command to Moses, \"Say to them\" (Numbers 14:28), was because he is the principal in prophecy."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The reading 'he would be in Moses' place' renders שיהיה הוא במקום משה, understood as a reference to Joshua's eventual succession."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:32.206153024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}